OL,3,GNEWSARopemaker says Traitors response
OL,4,A'fantastic'
OL,5,
OL,6,FA craftsman who made ropes used in the
OL,7,Fnew series of Celebrity Traitors says
OL,8,Fthe response has been "fantastic".
OL,10,FThe Westmorland Rope Company, based in
OL,11,FAppleby, installed the ropes on a
OL,12,Fshipwreck for the first challenge in
OL,13,Fthe BBC show, which saw celebrities
OL,14,Fincluding Miranda Hart, James Blunt and
OL,15,FRichard E Grant hunting for treasure.
OL,17,FIn Thursday's launch episode watched
OL,18,Flive by almost nine million people,
OL,19,FGrant and presenter Maya Jama were
OL,20,Fselected as two traitors, whose job is
OL,21,Fto plot the demise of fellow players.
OL,23,APub: 05-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,402,400,260,160,0,100
